585 0 obj
<<
/Title (Object counting is a core image-processing task used in industrial inspection, traffic monitoring, and more. It is achievable with just a Raspberry Pi, a camera, and Python/OpenCV [1].  Existing methods convert images to grayscale, which works under sharp contrast but fails when shadows or varying camera angles reduce visibility [1].  By switching to the LUV color space, we decouple lightness \(L\) from chromaticity \(u, v\), enabling more robust object detection where grayscale falls short [2].)
/Dest [9 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 518 0 R
>>
endobj
